 "manifesto": {
  "he": "כדי להיות ברור , הצום שלי התחיל מכך שפשוט - לא ידעתי מה לעשות ... אבל ידעתי שאני לא יכול לא לעשות כלום\n\nאם הודעה זו הגיע למישהו שלא מכיר את הטענה העיקרית - אז ככה:\n *הדרך היחידה לבטחון היא שלום* - למה ? כי בטחון אמיתי נמדד במבחן התוצאה של טווח הזמן - אם הוא לא לטווח ארוך זה לא נחשב - אשליה בטחונית שמשמרת את הרלוונטיות של עצמה לעד על ידי כח מייצרת את המצב כל שנה מחדש - מה, פשוט נמשיך עם מבצע כל קיץ ? כל כמה שנים נהיה מופתעים מחדש שתוקפים אותנו ? נמשיך במלחמה מתמדת ? שבאה בגלים כמו הים.. \nלא ... זה לא בטחון - זו לא הגנה אמיתית - צריך חוף מבטחים.. \nבטחון זה עידן שבוא אף אחד באמת לא תוקף אף אחד אחר. שכולם מבינים שלכולם כואב , שכולנו אחים (בנות ובני אברהם) לא בני דודים, שכל ילד הוא חף ותם , להבין באמת מה מסלים ומה מפייס , ולייצר היום את מחר, שבוא כל ילד וילדה בעולמנו יגדלו בשלווה... רק שלום אמיתי הוא בטחון אמיתי\n> ולמי שקצת התעמק על השיטה (שקשוקה) עלול להתעורר לכך שאולי כל זה - זה להסיך אותנו משאלות חשובות אחרות - כמו - למה הכל יקר כלכך ? ומה באמת קורה פה ? אבל זה רק קצה המזלג... תרתי משמע\n\n💜 אם אתם חושבים אחרת - אני מבין - מקווה לזכות לדבר איתכם בכבוד על הכל ולהבין אתכם טוב יותר - אני כל הזמן מכיר עוד אנשים שגדלו עם סיפורים לא עלינו וחוו חיים שאם אני הייתי נולד שם במקומם כמובן שהייתי מגיע לאותם מסקנות כמוהם -\nאין לי בהכרח את כל התשובות הנכונות, מקווה לשאול שאלות נכונות ,\nולאורר קצת אופטימיות",
  "en": "Hi everyone! Hope you are all well 🕊️✨\n\nWanted to share that I've (re)started a water only fast for about 10 to 14 days depending how it goes \n\nThis is going to be the 3rd year in a row that I'm doing this. Started when it was 1 yr memorial to October 7th \n\nThe idea is to fast for both a week Before till the week After 10.7 - to remember the pain of both sides, both preceding & leading up to it , and ever since...\n\nToday's October 1st I officially started the fast for peace again. And I'll shortly be heading to Tel-Aviv with a Suka-of-Peace\n\n📍 Sukkat-HaShalom at Habima Square, Tel Aviv · October 1 until around October 14\n\nTo be clear, my fast originally began simply because I didn't know what to do... but I knew I couldn't do nothing.\n\nA bit of background..\nI've traveled to a few places in my life where, before people got to know me the fact that I was a jewish israeli put me in real risk of dangerous. But as I've told them that I consider all of us sons of man and sons of Abraham, that we are all brothers, not cousins... They not only saw my heart, but gave me active protection. I've made real Syrian Persian and even Gazan friends, with a hug and the promise that soon enough our children will grow up together! \n\n\nSo for anyone reading this, here is my main argument (mainly from the perspective of one israeli to another):\n\n*The only path to security is peace.* Why? Because real security is measured by results over time. If it isn't long-term, it doesn't count. A security apparatus illusion that keeps itself relevant forever through force recreates the same situation year after year. What, do we just carry on with military operations every summer? Every few years we'll be surprised all over again that we're attacked? Will we keep the endless war forever - like waves like the sea...\nNo... that isn't security. That isn't real protection. We need a safe harbor...\nReal Security is an era in which no one  attacks anyone else. When everyone understands that everyone hurts, that we are all siblings (daughters and sons of Abraham), not cousins, that every child is innocent and pure. To truly understand what escalates and what reconciles, and to create tomorrow today, so that every boy and girl in our world grows up in peace... Only real peace is real security.\n> And for the initiated who have looked a little deeper into the system (shakshuka), it may dawn on you that maybe all of this is meant to distract us from other important questions, like: why is everything so expensive? And what is really going on behind the scenes? But that's just the tip of the fork... \n\nIf you think differently, I understand.. Hope we get a chance to talk  respectfully about everything and to understand each other better. I keep meeting more people who grew up with stories I wouldn't wish on anyone and lived lives where, had I been born in their place, of course I would have reached the same conclusions they did.\nI don't necessarily have all the right answers. I hope to ask the right questions..\nand to bring in a little optimism to the table\n\n\n\nJust for context..\nI was born in Israel, and to me Zion (the ancient name long before Israel/Palestine) is not the Promised Land, but the Promised TIME - where everybody living in the Present, in actual real Peace and harmony - that's my chosen interpretation.\n\nBased on my travels and seeing regardless of culture how all humans are very alike.. I understand that one of the biggest reasons this conflict is prolonged so much is because we are segregated, and not allowed to meet each other, people to people. (and obviously a lot of money and influence to keep the status quo..)\n\nSo until we have real disarmament on both sides and maybe a million people marching together to open up the borders, I'll do what I can on this side of the wire, and try to get people back to optimism and hope that the age of peace, the promised times, just might be soon upon us, God willing\n\nIf anyone has any contacts in TLV and can send some angels my way that would be greatly appreciated 🙏😇\nAnd if you're far away: share this, fast with me for one day, or send a short video of support 🙏\n\nThanks a lot and all the best! Jah bless & Peace upon us 🕊️✨"
 },
